From 41b0c2dce36775225b0b8caeb389e13438afdc3b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex Unleashed <codex-unleashed@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 04:18:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] test: Keep interrupt-hook host cwd independent of tool
 execution

Keep an owned host configuration directory while preserving explicit executor selection and workspace callbacks. Default fixture behavior remains unchanged. Reject unsupported legacy resume and shell overrides before startup.

Fixture checks reproduce three boundary failures before the change and pass all six cases after it. Five local interrupt scenarios pass with the host-hook production repair (issue-61 0080); Docker and Wine execution remain unverified.
